quran[26]{c,v,t}:
  69,9,Then Pharaoh and those before him and the overthrown towns (of the community of Lut) committed grave sins.
  69,10,They (also) disobeyed the messenger of their Lord. So He seized them with a terrible crushing grip.
  69,11,"Indeed, when the flood water rose high, We carried you in the floating ship,"
  69,12,"so that We make it a reminder for you, and attentive ears may grasp it."
  69,13,"When the Trumpet is blown with a single blast,"
  69,14,"and the earth and the mountains are lifted and crushed (into sand particles) with a single blow,"
  69,15,"on that Day, the Inevitable event will occur."
  69,16,"The heavenly universe shall split asunder. So, (by losing its force) it will become torn into holes.*"
  69,17,"And the angels shall be (standing) at its edges. On that Day, eight (mighty angels) will carry the Throne of your Lord above them."
  69,18,"That Day, you will be exposed. None of your secrets will remain hidden."
  69,19,"As for the one given his book in his right hand, he will say (happily): ‘Come here and read my book!"
  69,20,I knew that I would surely face my reckoning.’
  69,21,"So he will have a pleasant life,"
  69,22,"in an elevated garden,"
  69,23,whose clusters of fruit will be low-hanging (within easy reach).
  69,24,(They will be told:) ‘Enjoy your food and drink for what you had sent in advance in the past days.’
  69,25,"But as for the one given his book in his left hand, he will say: ‘I wish I had not been given my book,"
  69,26,nor had I known what my account was!
  69,27,I wish death had been the decisive end (of all affairs).
  69,28,My wealth has not benefited me.
  69,29,My authority has departed from me.’
  69,30,(The angels will be told:) ‘Seize him and shackle him.
  69,31,Then put him into Hellfire.
  69,32,"Then tie him up in a chain, seventy arms long."
  69,33,"Indeed, he did not believe in Allah, the Most Magnificent,"
  69,34,nor did he encourage the feeding of the needy.
